UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'AN EVIDENCE RETRIEVAL MADE THROUGH WebFetch LEAVES NO ARTEFACT, AND THE RECORD CANNOT TELL. CLAUDE.md section 5(c): verification must leave an artefact, and scripts/research/retrieval_log.py persists every payload before returning. WebFetch and WebSearch bypass it entirely. Measured on this batch: exec 72 records seven routes; ten attempts were made, three of them through WebFetch/WebSearch and therefore unpersisted -- and one of those three is the HTTP 503 that the session record then RETRACTED as never having happened, because the only evidence for it was the harness transcript. So an unpersisted retrieval produced a false claim, a false retraction of that claim, and no way to settle either without reading the transcript. WHAT WOULD FIX IT: retrieval_log.fetch as the only sanctioned route for evidence retrieval, with the tool-level alternatives named as forbidden in the research contract; or a check comparing a search_execution''s asserted route count against persisted artefacts, which needs an exec-to-artefact edge that does not exist. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: GAP-088 extends this to the WebSearch tool and to linking a payload to a search whose query text does not name its host.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:05', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-034';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'scripts/db.py''s _require_verbatim digit-check (add-extraction''s claimed_value verification, ~line 6579) was widened 2026- to accept CJK numerals alongside Arabic digits, but has no path for LATIN-SCRIPT SPELLED-OUT CARDINAL NUMBERS -- e.g. Finnish ''viisi prosenttia''/''kahdeksan prosenttia'' (five/eight percent), which is how Finland''s Decree 241/2017 states its ramp-gradient figures throughout (no digit form appears anywhere in the statute text). A claimed_value written in digit form (''5%'') is refused because no digit character occurs in the verified claim_text; --verbatim-exempt cannot rescue it either, because exemption is refused whenever the claim_text DOES verify against a persisted artefact (it does here). Net effect: a genuinely verbatim-verified numerical claim from a language that spells cardinals as words has NO path to carry a digit-form claimed_value at all. Worked around in batch 22 (REF-01017, Finland, extraction on parameter 3) by setting claimed_value to the source''s own spelled-out form (''viisi prosenttia'') and giving the digit-equivalent only as an editorial gloss in --claimed-unit/--notes, explicitly marked as non-verbatim. Fix belongs in a tooling-only PR (rule 10): extend the digit-check with a small per-language cardinal-number lexicon (or a number-parsing library) analogous to the existing _CJK_DIGITS/_CJK_UNITS tables, or provide an explicit escape that documents a spelled-out-to-digit mapping without requiring the exemption path. R5 (non-English work is academic, not lesser) applies here exactly as it did for the CJK fix this function''s own comment already describes. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: GAP-090 is the same class for Korean line breaks: a quote cannot cross a break inside a word.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:05', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-056';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'NOTHING PROMOTES A HARVESTED TERM TO A PARAMETER, SO EVERY BATCH IS CONFINED TO THE ONE PARAMETER THAT EXISTS. source_value_extractions.parameter_id is NOT NULL and a real FK into base_parameters, which holds one live row (3, ramp gradient); every extraction in the database is filed under it. The path from an encountered concept to a parameter exists and works (observe-term, add-term --from-observation, add-parameter; the adjudication gate was deliberately dropped from add-parameter so it cannot block), and the first two steps run every batch (derive: select count(*) from terms, base_parameters, observed_terms, term_adjudications). The third does not: TERM-091 ramp run length and TERM-092 intermediate landing were adjudicated NAMES-NEW and never promoted. No rule in the research contract, none in research_batch_dod.py, no command under .claude/commands and no skill under .claude/skills mentions promotion, and no check compares what a source states with the parameters that exist. Consequence: a source read in full yields rows for one parameter only (batch 23: 14 building-regulation sources, 30 extractions, all parameter 3; widths, run lengths, landing dimensions, handrail and material provisions captured at most as an observed term or one code lead) and everything else needs a second read. Measured on a scratch copy 2026-10-01: promoting four existing terms (door width, level threshold, ramp run length, intermediate landing) tripped no content check; test_db_integrity stayed at its single D04 failure. Remedy is a tooling-only PR merged first (rule 10): a contract rule (a figure for a concept with no parameter is minted in the same batch) and a research_batch_dod report of NAMES-NEW terms with no parameter, derived not listed. Whether a neutral seed list drawn from the retired item names is permitted is a separate owner question; the owner''s recorded objection has two strands (names that embed a determination, DR-2026-08-19 1.1; pre-existing containers). Minting as sources raise concepts needs neither. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: The parameter promotion path now exists (add-parameter); GAP-078 records that parameters 7 and 10 still hold no row.', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:05', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-061';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'COMPOSITION OF PARAMETER 12 REFUSES MIXED LENGTH UNITS. assess_cell.NOTATION_FAMILIES holds only the gradient family, so compose_value over parameter 12''s governing claims returns NULL with ''stated in different units'' as soon as one source states centimetres and another metres, and the only value that composes drops the gentlest figure. Reproduce: python3 -I -c with compose_value(con, [{''role'':''governing'',''extraction_id'':e} for e in <ids of parameter 12 rows>], ''lower_is_better''). Not repaired here: a tooling change ships in its own PR (rule 10). The rows keep the unit each source states. || CORRECTED 2026-10-31: [2026-10-30, session_2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages-rebuild] The rows this session added to parameter 12 state their figures in metres or millimetres (never prose in the unit field), so they compose under the length family once the engine owns one; the same refusal applies to them until it does. || CORRECTED 2026-11-06: GAP-094 extends this: parameters 4, 6, 9 and 11 now also hold rows in m, cm, mm and N (session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch and -2).', "updated_at" = '2026-11-06 05:05', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-11-06-pipeline-batch-2' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-072';